      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T12:48:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be concrete, the below sample change in mainloop aims to fix it. Basically in most cases, we only handle the state change (with `modify_state`) in the `action_xxxx` functions, and the mainloop only logs the result or triggers callbacks.\n\nHowever to log the result inside mainloop we have to either (1) query the result with `get_state` or (2) let the `action_xxxx` functions return the next state. (2) is already used in some other places in this file (refer to `StartBluetooth` and `HciDevicePresence`) thus I chose it.\n```\n-next_state \u003d ProcessState::TurningOff;\n-let action \u003d context.state_machine.action_stop_bluetooth(hci);\n+let action;\n+(next_state, action) \u003d context.state_machine.action_stop_bluetooth(hci);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "18ef38a2_fdf45b44",
